        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.5.3 (open).
            Proof IDs: PROOF-001, PROOF-008, PROOF-009, PROOF-010, PROOF-011, PROOF-012, PROOF-013.
            Deliverable: Story commands, virtual time, occurrences, immutable checkpoints,
            failure evidence, and run.end through the production mailbox and kernels.
            Derived plans replay shared prefixes in fresh production Runtimes.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/stories/**.
            Public routes and package facades belong to Phase 6 entrypoint ownership.
            Evidence: Owner behavior tests and checkpoint type proofs, with command results.
            Absorbs Story command, checkpoint, failure, and cleanup proof lanes from closed
            Bead flow-state-e7p.5.7.
            Phase 4 validation T405 must pass before this work starts.
        acceptance
            send waits only for its own acknowledgment; process and time movement stay separate.
            Checkpoint creation advances no work. Failed runs retain completed checkpoints and
            never fabricate success or run.end.
            Cancellation records truthful evidence and ordered cleanup.
            Checkpoint names accumulate in exact run keys; invalid names and unknown lookup reject.
            No simulation, replay, result injection, or live Runtime fork is exposed.
            Positive and negative type fixtures preserve checkpoint-name and run-result types.
            Run `nubx vp test packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/stories/tests`,
            `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types`, `nub run test`, and
            `nub run lint`. Expected: all checks pass.
    T503
        title        Behavior gateway, fixtures, and model parity
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T501, @T502, @task.Rewrite.T404, @task.Rewrite.T405]

        derives_from [
                     @plan.CLI.D1,
                     @plan.CLI.C1,
                     @plan.CLI.C2,
                     @plan.CLI.V1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V5,
                     @plan.Artifacts.D1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.D2,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C2,
                     @plan.Types.V6,
                     @plan.Types.V7,
                     @plan.PublicSurface.V5,
                     @plan.Verification.V4,
                     @plan.Verification.V6
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.Artifacts.O7]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.5.4 (open).
            Proof IDs: PROOF-008, PROOF-011, API-P03.
            Deliverable: An inert single-App gateway, validated fixture services and seeds,
            pure bounded model traversal, and live parity through ordinary Stories. Model paths
            use the Story-owned production capture only when their ordinary Story runs.
            Keep gateway, fixture, model, and Story owners cohesive with local tests.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/stories/** and
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/model/**.
            Public routes and package facades belong to Phase 6 entrypoint ownership.
            Evidence: Gateway rejection tests, deterministic BFS/DFS model tests, and live parity
            receipts from production owners.
            Absorbs the gateway and live parity proof lanes from closed Bead
            flow-state-e7p.5.7.
            Phase 4 validation T405 must pass before this work starts.
        acceptance
            Gateway validation acquires or runs nothing and rejects mixed or foreign content.
            The model imports or executes no Effect, Runtime, fixture, or operation.
            BFS returns bounded shortest paths; DFS returns bounded simple paths with accurate
            explored counts and truncation.
            Repeated model calls retain no candidates; live hosts and Stories share production
            owners.
            A checkpoint and `run.end` capture one DehydrateBarrier cut with exact actor targets,
            pending work, TestClock time, Store revision, published snapshots, and accepted prefix.
            App evidence resolves storyActor or ActorRef; machine evidence exposes one snapshot.
            `run.end` is evidence completion, never actor finality.
            Capture advances no work or time and never creates, disposes, restores, or reads
            a live actor.
            Failed runs retain completed checkpoints and truthful cleanup.
            Cancellation closes admission, preserves partial evidence, awaits non-abortable cleanup,
            then fails.
            Success implies complete disposal; capture or cleanup failure never fabricates
            `run.end` or success. FlowStoryExecutionError retains complete public Cause only in
            process.
            A model accepts only a fresh, command-empty machine Story and stays Effect-free.
            Discovery processes no work or time; it creates, restores, or looks up no actor and
            does no external work. Candidates stay traversal-local; no replay is added.
            Path Stories use ordinary production owners and capture only when run.
            Positive and negative type fixtures keep model inputs, paths, and candidates exact.
            Run `nubx vp test packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/model/tests` and
            `nubx vp test packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/stories/tests`, then
            `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types`, `nub run test`, and
            `nub run lint`. Expected: all checks pass.
