                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.CLI.O1]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.5.5 (open).
            Proof IDs: CLI-P01, CLI-012, PROOF-014, API-P03.
            Deliverable: The exact CLI grammar, trusted contained gateway loader, and one shared
            direct and CLI Story executor.
            Artifact-only commands remain inert; gateway validation uses shared diagnostics.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/cli/**.
            Update only the CLI call site for the Story-owned executor.
            Evidence: CLI grammar and gateway tests, direct/CLI parity tests, and lint receipts.
            Absorbs gateway and executor proof lanes from closed Bead flow-state-e7p.5.7.
            Phase 4 validation T405 must pass before this work starts.
        acceptance
            Only the ten leaves in CLI.plan are accepted; options and operands are exact.
            Selector parsing loads no gateway; artifact-only commands execute no application.
            Gateway paths stay under the canonical project root and resolve to a regular TS file.
            Package identity and branded gateway checks reject before acquisition.
            All Story execution uses the production executor and shared diagnostics.
            Run `nubx vp test packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/cli/tests`,
            `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types`, `nub run test`, and
            `nub run lint`. Expected: all checks pass.
    T505
        title        CLI artifacts, publication, streams, and exits
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T504, @T508, @task.Rewrite.T405]

        derives_from [
                     @plan.CLI.D1,
                     @plan.CLI.D2,
                     @plan.CLI.D3,
                     @plan.CLI.C1,
                     @plan.CLI.C2,
                     @plan.CLI.C3,
                     @plan.CLI.V2,
                     @plan.CLI.V3,
                     @plan.CLI.V4,
                     @plan.Artifacts.D1,
                     @plan.Artifacts.C3,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V3,
                     @plan.Artifacts.V5,
                     @plan.PublicSurface.V6,
                     @plan.Verification.V6
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.CLI.O2, @plan.CLI.O3]
        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.5.6 (open).
            Proof IDs: CLI-P01, PROOF-010, PROOF-014.
            Deliverable: Bounded artifact input, canonical results, atomic publication, document
            output, stream failures, signal cleanup, and exact process exits.
            Reuse the shared artifact codecs and CLI executor.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/cli/**.
            Shared artifact codecs and package facades remain owned by their existing Tasks.
            Evidence: Input boundary, publication, process, and interruption tests plus lint.
            Absorbs artifact and CLI parity proof lanes from closed Bead flow-state-e7p.5.7.
            Phase 4 validation T405 must pass before this work starts.
        acceptance
            Use the shared codec; accept one stdin operand or named regular files only. Destination
            preflight finishes before Runtime or Fixture acquisition.
            Reject malformed, oversized, multi-member, and legacy artifact inputs before acquire.
            Publish through a mode-0600 sibling temporary file; flush and close before commit.
            No-overwrite uses atomic link; overwrite uses atomic rename without truncation.
            Replacing a symlink changes its entry, never its referent; pre-commit failure preserves
            the prior or absent destination.
            Share artifacts reject as WrongArtifactKind and never enter CLI, import, replay,
            or boot.
            One private result drives text and JSON; each stream is one complete write with no
            stdout/stderr mixing. EPIPE performs no recursive write.
            Success emits one stdout document; failure emits one stderr document.
            Exit codes are 0, 1, 2, 130, or 143 as specified by CLI.plan.
            Signal cleanup retains evidence and attempts requested partial-trace output. Trace
            summaries and comparisons preserve incomplete-window truth.
            Direct and CLI runs share Story/evidence owners; parity covers `run.end`, failure, and
            cancellation. Arbitrary event fabrication rejects.
            Human text stays actionable, newline-terminated, and ANSI-free when non-interactive.
            Run `nubx vp test packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/cli/tests`,
            `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types`, `nub run test`, and
            `nub run lint`. Expected: all checks pass.
