        description
            Source Bead: flow-state-e7p.5.8 (open); source epic: flow-state-e7p.5 (open).
            Deliverable: Independent, read-only review of changed Phase 5 slices and named Plan
            checks after implementation owners pass.
            Review only changed diffs and their production-owner evidence; do not re-audit other
            phases or duplicate proof matrices.
            Allowed writes: none for reviewers. Return the required handback in the Task result.
            Evidence: Exact changed paths, focused check commands and results, proof coverage,
            findings, and lint result in the handback.
            Retired tracker flow-state-e7p.5.7 (closed) is absorbed by T500-T505; closure was
            administrative and did not pass its proof obligations.
            Phase 4 validation T405 gates the implementation Tasks in this phase.
        acceptance
            Return these fields: contract references, changed files, focused checks, lint result,
            behavior reviewed, fixed findings, blocking findings, advisory findings.
            Review proof coverage and reachability through production owners.
            Confirm no blocking findings, duplicate authority, hidden compatibility path, partial
            mutation, or type erasure remains in the changed Phase 5 slices.
            Review T500-T505 and T507-T508, repeat their focused checks, then run `nub run lint`.
            Expected: all checks pass and no blocking findings remain.

    T507
        title        Integrate Effect bridges and trusted host writes
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T500, @T508, @task.Rewrite.T305, @task.Rewrite.T405]
        derives_from @plan.Hosts.{D1,D2,C2,V4}
        satisfies    [@plan.Hosts.O6]
        description
            Workflow addition: no live source Bead maps to this production Effect bridge and
            host integration; retain it as new Workflow work.
            Reuse StoreKernel's private HostWriteLease from P3; do not create a second lease
            owner or runner. Keep the bridge and its tests under
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/hosts/.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/hosts/**.

            Run Effects with the installed Runtime Context and retain the complete Exit through
            cleanup. Keep reusable services in exact Effect A, Diagnostic E, and R. Adapt each
            foreign Promise once with a named `Effect.tryPromise` adapter and forward AbortSignal
            where supported. Integrate the scoped lease for boot, SSR, and Fixture seeding.
            Public routes remain owned by Phase 6.
        acceptance
            Bridges use the installed Runtime Context; `runPromiseExit` retains the complete Exit
            and Implementation/runtime failure truth without a second Scope.
            Rejected Promises map to owned Diagnostics with and without AbortSignal support.
            Only the owner mints a lease for its AppPlan, Runtime, and allowed boundary.
            Foreign, stale, revoked, and wrong-boundary leases fail before StoreState mutation.
            Valid writes use admitted descriptors and `K` through StoreKernel fencing, revision,
            fanout, and authoritative-write rules.
            Scope close and Runtime disposal revoke the lease.
            Run `nubx vp test packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/hosts/tests`,
            `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types`, and `nub run lint`. All pass.

    T508
        title        Implement canonical diagnostics and failure mapping
        status       draft
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@task.Rewrite.T306, @task.Rewrite.T405]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Diagnostics.D1,
                     @plan.Diagnostics.D2,
                     @plan.Diagnostics.C1,
                     @plan.Diagnostics.C2,
                     @plan.Diagnostics.C3,
                     @plan.Diagnostics.V1,
                     @plan.Diagnostics.V2,
                     @plan.Diagnostics.V3,
                     @plan.Diagnostics.V4,
                     @plan.PublicSurface.V6,
                     @plan.Verification.V6,
                     @plan.Types.V6,
                     @plan.Types.V7
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.Diagnostics.O1, @plan.Diagnostics.O2, @plan.Diagnostics.O3]
        description
            Workflow addition: no live source Bead maps to this diagnostic owner; retain it as
            new Workflow work. Implement the Schema-backed Diagnostic owner from the migrated
            Task requirements. `reference/incident-console/implementation/contracts/ERRORS.ts`
            is a historical source citation, not active authority for diagnostic behavior.
            Historical source amendment: AMEND-API-002. Proof ID: AMEND-P03.
            Keep code and owner tests under packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/diagnostic/.
            Create the usage-code remediation table at
            apps/docs/src/pages/reference/diagnostics.mdx.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/diagnostic/** and
            apps/docs/src/pages/reference/diagnostics.mdx.

            Implement structural decode, semantic Result mapping, typed Effect mapping, and
            private Exit/Cause classification with exact A/R preservation. Add the synchronous
            usage boundary and renderer. Keep deferred names absent from active package routes;
            Public facade changes remain owned by Phase 6. Do not edit the cited historical
            contract file or change diagnostic behavior through this Task.
        acceptance
            Diagnostic has exact fields, closed code/reason sets, path/details domains, and encoded
            type. It is a TaggedError, Error, Schema codec, and directly yieldable Effect failure.
            Structural decoding returns plain data and maps only SchemaError. Result mapping
            preserves A; Effect mapping preserves A and R.
            Cause classification preserves Exit and Cause through cleanup; precedence is defect,
            typed failure, then interruption-only.
            Cause.squash occurs only at a lossy synchronous JavaScript host boundary.
            Only FlowDisposeError and FlowStoryExecutionError carry complete Cause, in process.
            DiagnosticPrinter exposes compact/pretty; renderDiagnosticCompact and
            renderDiagnosticPretty are shared policy exports.
            Serialized diagnostics contain no Cause; projections remain ordered and stable.
            Rendering receives only Diagnostic fields and exposes no raw input or Cause.
            FlowUsageError has exact tag/code/path/details and accepts only UsageDiagnostic.
            FlowPersistenceError has no extra fields; the exact 18 usage codes each have a
            path/details and remediation row. Messages stay non-API.
            Deferred names retain their declarations and remain absent from active root exports.
            Run diagnostic and public-route tests, package type and packed-consumer checks,
            `nub run docs:build`, and `nub run lint`. All pass.
